{"name":"Waterscape","hex":"#dcece7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"waterscape","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An aquatic landscape; a view or site prominently involving water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To create an aquatic landscape."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waterscape"}],"entries":[{"title":"British Waterways","blocks":[{"text":"British Waterways, often shortened to BW, was a statutory corporation wholly owned by the government of the United Kingdom. It served as the navigation authority for the majority of canals and a number of rivers and docks in England, Scotland and Wales."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Waterways"},{"title":"San Jose City Hall","blocks":[{"text":"San José City Hall is the seat of the municipal government of San Jose, California. Located in Downtown San Jose, it was designed by Pritzker Prize-winning architect Richard Meier in a Postmodern style. It consists of an 18-story tower, an iconic glass rotunda, and a city council chamber wing, laid out within a two-block-long public square known as San José Civic Plaza. The tower rises 285 feet (87 m) above the plaza, making it the fourth tallest building in San Jose."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Sanjosecityhall.jpg/330px-Sanjosecityhall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Jose_City_Hall"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/British_Waterways_sign_Birmingham_-_2004.jpg/500px-British_Waterways_sign_Birmingham_-_2004.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/British_Waterways_sign_Birmingham_-_2004.jpg/1280px-British_Waterways_sign_Birmingham_-_2004.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wi